  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The float returned for the player's eye height when OnAvatarEyeHeightChanged is called is derived from the player's current head position relative to the avatar's 0 position, rather than where it would be in a standing t-pose calibration like it should. \n\nThis means players in full-body tracking produce results well off the intended mark, as their tracked eye-height value can be much lower \n\n(eg;  If you change avatars while sitting or laying down, it will return the position of your head in that position when the avatar loads as the current eye-height.)",
